\newlabel{fig:shuffle-network}{{1}{2}{Shuffle-Exchange network routing signals from 8 input sequence addresses (sequence element locations) from the left to 8 output sequence addresses to the right. Each green block is a Switch Unit that takes two input elements and either swaps or leaves them unchanged. A column of Switch Units forms a Switch Layer. The arrows between two Switch Layers represent a Shuffle Layer that permutes the elements. In this figure, the switches are configured to route an element from address 000 to 111. }{}{}}
